DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The vvmm__ppaaggee__ffrreeee__ttooqq() function moves a page into the free queue, and
     disassociates it from its object.  If the page is held, wired, already
     free, or its busy count is not zero, the system will panic.  If the
     PG_ZERO flag is set on the page, it is placed at the end of the free
     queue; otherwise, it is placed at the front.

     If the page's object is of type OBJT_VNODE and it is the last page asso‐
     ciated with the object, the underlying vnode may be freed.

     The vvmm__ppaaggee__ffrreeee() and vvmm__ppaaggee__ffrreeee__zzeerroo() functions both call
     vvmm__ppaaggee__ffrreeee__ttooqq() to actually free the page, but vvmm__ppaaggee__ffrreeee__zzeerroo()
     sets the PG_ZERO flag and vvmm__ppaaggee__ffrreeee() clears the PG_ZERO flag prior to
     the call to vvmm__ppaaggee__ffrreeee__ttooqq().

     The vvmm__ppaaggee__ttrryy__ttoo__ffrreeee() function verifies that the page is not held,
     wired, busy or dirty, and if so, marks the page as busy, drops any pro‐
     tection that may be set on the page, and frees it.

RREETTUURRNN VVAALLUUEESS
     vvmm__ppaaggee__ttrryy__ttoo__ffrreeee() returns 1 if it is able to free the page; other‐
     wise, 0 is returned.

